WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:05.910
This diagram illustrates a staggering reality in modern health care.

2
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.210
For some of the 10 highest-grossing drugs in the United States,

3
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:13.330
only 1 in 25 patients actually benefits from the treatment.

4
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.410
At best, that number improves to 1 in 4.

5
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.250
The math breaks down because the entire pharmaceutical pipeline is built around an entity

6
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.550
that doesn't actually exist in nature,

7
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.270
the average patient.

8
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.710
Clinical trials compress thousands of unique metabolisms and genetic profiles into a single

9
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:31.790
statistical mean.

10
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.130
This widespread failure rate isn't a medical mystery.

11
00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.770
It stems directly from two distinct mechanical bottlenecks and how we administer drugs,

12
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.270
how they physically reach a cell, and how we time the dose.

13
00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.250
As long as the medical infrastructure relies on that single one-size-fits-all assumption,

14
00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:51.610
treatments will continue to break down at both of these exact points.

15
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.290
Solving this crisis requires abandoning the average patient model entirely,

16
00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.350
both in the physical way a drug enters the tissue and the rigid timeline of how it is

17
00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:01.850
prescribed.

18
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.490
The first bottleneck is physical delivery.

19
00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:08.050
Standard lipid nanoparticles are essentially blind packages.

20
00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:13.070
They ignore the specific receptor expressions of a patient's cellular microenvironment,

21
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:16.750
failing to penetrate the target tissue and simply degrading in the bloodstream.

22
00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.330
The second bottleneck is static dosing.

23
00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:25.330
Currently, a physician derives a fixed prescription based on a single snapshot in time,

24
00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.310
a brief clinic visit or a solitary blood draw.

25
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.890
That model assumes your internal biology stays perfectly flat between appointments.

26
00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.330
In reality, your receptor availability,

27
00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.950
inflammation levels, and metabolic rates fluctuate constantly.

28
00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:45.530
Instructional Biology addresses both of these flaws through a platform called MET-APFS,

29
00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:50.030
a system designed to treat the individual rather than the statistical average.

30
00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.230
They achieve this by splitting the problem in half.

31
00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:58.470
They decoupled the physical delivery vehicle from its ongoing digital regulation, creating

32
00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.010
two distinct technologies that can be licensed across the entire industry.

33
00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.710
The physical solution is the Markosian exosomal transcytosis system, or MET.

34
00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.830
These carriers are highly specific.

35
00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:13.710
Before a single exosome is loaded, it goes through an outer design loop.

36
00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:18.830
A machine learning model computes a configuration record tailored to the patient, identifying

37
00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:23.170
the exact targeting ligand needed before the manufacturing apparatus even turns on.

38
00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.670
This 3D model demonstrates the system's core commercial advantage.

39
00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.470
The MET exosome is completely payload-agnostic.

40
00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.190
As you can see, the complex engineering required to target specific cells on the outside

41
00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:40.510
is entirely separate from the proprietary cargo loaded on the inside.

42
00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.750
This creates a direct commercial pathway.

43
00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:48.130
A third-party biotech company can license the MET system to deliver their own vulnerable

44
00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:53.470
RNA, proteins, or small molecules without having to invent a new delivery vehicle from

45
00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:53.790
scratch.

46
00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:59.590
It turns cell-specific drug delivery from a bespoke, highly risky science experiment into

47
00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:02.150
reliable plug-and-play physical infrastructure.

48
00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.310
Once the drug enters the body, the inner administration loop takes over.

49
00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:11.970
This is governed by the Autonomic Pharmacokinetic Feedback System, or APFS, which solves

50
00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:14.230
the temporal bottleneck of static dosing.

51
00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:19.950
APFS pulls continuous physiological data from consumer wearables, like smartwatches and

52
00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:24.030
rings, which have been specifically calibrated against clinical reference sensors for

53
00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.130
that individual patient.

54
00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:29.470
That continuous data feed powers a patient-specific digital twin.

55
00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:36.310
This model calculates the individual's unique biological state, and predicts exactly how

56
00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.590
they will respond to the medication over time.

57
00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.290
Take a look at this trajectory graph.

58
00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:46.390
It plots the twin's predicted response against the patient's measured reality.

59
00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:51.930
The moment those lines diverge, the system automatically calculates a revised dose or

60
00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:52.970
a new dosing interval.

61
00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:58.230
To prevent algorithmic hallucinations and ensure absolute safety,

62
00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.630
notice this rigid bounding box.

63
00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.910
This is the prescriber authorization envelope.

64
00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:08.830
It contains hard upper and lower limits, cryptographically signed by a doctor.

65
00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:13.810
Automated adjustments only execute if they fall strictly within this envelope.

66
00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:16.350
If a computed revision hits the boundary,

67
00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:20.250
the command turns red, the rejection is logged to an immutable ledger,

68
00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:24.950
and the local safety controller instantly drops the device to a safe basal rate.

69
00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:30.350
Because this digital safety net operates independently of the exosome carrier,

70
00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:36.610
APFS can be licensed to dynamically regulate entirely unrelated third-party therapies

71
00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:38.530
across the pharmaceutical sector.

72
00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.550
Within Instructional Biology's own pipeline,

73
00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:48.710
MET and APFS work together to bridge the massive gap between population averages and individual

74
00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:49.350
patients.

75
00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:53.690
As the schematic shows, their disruptive value comes from independence.

76
00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.330
The central stack powers internal therapeutics,

77
00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:00.690
while the horizontal axis enables external licensing.

78
00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.350
Pharma companies can lease the MET carrier to salvage stalled assets,

79
00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:11.210
and trial sponsors can separately license the APFS digital twin for personalized dosing.

80
00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.250
Partners acquire exactly what they need.

81
00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:19.150
They are never forced to adopt the company's entire manufacturing and intelligence stack

82
00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:22.050
just to benefit from one specific capability.

83
00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:25.590
By decoupling the vehicle from the algorithm,

84
00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:31.610
Instructional Biology offers modular infrastructure, where biological packaging and digital

85
00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:34.410
regulation finally adapt to the individual.

